.page cd 1 change the working directory

# SYNOPSIS
*cd* [_DIRECTORY_ | *-*]

# DESCRIPTION
`cd` is a gapsh builtin. It changes the current directory to _DIRECTORY_, or to the home directory (`$HOME`) if none is given. `cd -` goes back to the previous directory (`$OLDPWD`) and prints its name. `PWD` and `OLDPWD` are updated.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if the directory does not exist, is not a directory or is not accessible, or `HOME` or `OLDPWD` is not set.

# EXAMPLES
    cd /Hakurei/etc
    cd
    cd -

# SEE ALSO
pwd(1), pushd(1), gapsh-builtins(7)
